# Scratch work, not the project.
#
# Everything here is UNSHIPPED: one-shot probes written to answer one
# question, mutation tables written to prove the suite bites, their captured
# output, and the UI sketches the build was designed against. Not part of the
# build, not something anybody should have to read, and they must never reach
# a commit.
#
# The convention is the leading underscore, and it is the whole rule: a file
# named _anything is scratch. Everything without one is the project. It is the
# same rule judgement and the rest of the family use, so a file moved between
# the repos keeps its meaning.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNSHIPPED IS NOT THE SAME AS DISPOSABLE. DO NOT BULK-DELETE BY THE PATTERN.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The underscore says "git does not carry this". It does not say "nobody needs
# this". One of these files is load-bearing:
#
#   scripts/_mutate.mjs     THE MUTATION TABLE. Every rule the brief's
#                           definition of done lists has rows in it, and it is
#                           how each one was shown to be CAUGHT rather than
#                           merely made to pass. Run it before trusting a green
#                           suite after touching js/. There is no command that
#                           rebuilds it.
#
# The sketches (_sketch*.html) are the designs the UI was built against. They
# use `sk-` prefixed scaffold classes so they cannot inherit app.css rules —
# see the brief's lesson 14, which is a judgement sketch that reused `.panel`
# and reported a regression that existed only in the sketch.
#
# CAPTURED OUTPUT IS DELETED ON SIGHT. A redirected run log is a transcript of
# one execution of something that is still on disk and still runnable, and a
# stale one reads as evidence for a version of the code that no longer exists.
#
# NOT ignored, and deliberately so:
#   scripts/test-engine.mjs   the suite itself
#   scripts/domshim.mjs       the DOM the suite renders into, headless
#   scripts/peershim.mjs      the transport the suite talks over, headless
#   scripts/gen-icons.js      generates icons/, which ships
#
# The check that nothing has fallen between the two lists:
#
#     git ls-files --others --exclude-standard     # must print nothing
_*

# Editor/session state.
.claude/

# OS and editor litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# There are no dependencies — package.json has no "dependencies" key and the
# page loads ES modules straight from js/. node_modules/ should never appear;
# it is listed so that if some tool creates one, it is not committed by
# somebody who did not notice.
node_modules/
